Arara Code: browser-compatible language detection entry point.

Why a patch: the built-in language detection worker is outside extension APIs.
Its dependency ships a Node-targeted Webpack chunk loader that calls require in
workers. The prepare script emits an AMD-compatible entry with the shipped local
chunks in a scoped loader, preserving source and license notices. This patch
selects that entry for browser workers; no global Node API is exposed.
Touches: src/vs/workbench/services/languageDetection/browser/languageDetectionWorkerServiceImpl.ts

--- a/src/vs/workbench/services/languageDetection/browser/languageDetectionWorkerServiceImpl.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/services/languageDetection/browser/languageDetectionWorkerServiceImpl.ts
@@ -75,8 +75,8 @@
